General Corporate Law. This code does not include a definition of this term and
Maryland case law suggests that the term be defined on a case-by-case basis. The
effect of the Maryland law's lack of a definition of cause is that we cannot
provide investors with a definition for "cause." As a result of this
uncertainty, investors may not know what actions by a director may be grounds
for removal.

